    {
      "id": "b4",
      "function": "explanation",
      "scene_type": "rv_cutaway",
      "spoken": "The reason is the con rod. It runs at an angle and links the piston to the crank pin. In the upper half of the stroke, that angle pulls the piston down even faster. In the lower half, the same angle slows it down earlier.",
      "data": {
        "title": "The angled con rod",
        "speed": true,
        "labels": [
