      "function": "insight",
      "scene_type": "rv_chart",
      "spoken": "According to the engineering lecture, the peak in typical car engines sits at about seventy degrees after top dead centre. In our model it is seventy-four degrees, clearly before mid-stroke. So the curve is not symmetrical: a quick start at the top, a gentler finish at the bottom.",
